<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#chariot">Glossary</a> · Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chariot</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A chariot is a light, two-wheeled, horse-drawn vehicle used in warfare, carrying a driver and an archer or spearman. Chariots were decisive weapons in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a>, used by the Egyptian Empire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire</a>, renowned for their horse training. They remained in use by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> and in early Indian warfare, including the Maurya army.</p></div>
